**The Anglican Formularies** are historic documents that explain the faith and practice of the Anglican tradition. They provide a clear introduction to Anglican theology, worship, and the Christian life.

Explore three foundational resources: **To Be A Christian: An Anglican Catechism**, **The Book of Common Prayer**, and the **Thirty-Nine Articles of Religion**. Together they help explain what Anglicans believe, how we worship, and how we live out the Christian faith.

Anglican belief is also grounded in the historic **Apostles'**, **Nicene**, and **Athanasian Creeds**, which summarize the core truths of the Christian faith confessed by the Church throughout the centuries.
